  "instruction_layer": {
    "inline": [
      "The compiled runtime guide is authoritative for the next legal action.",
      "Observer owns orchestration, cardinality-aware dispatch (two atomic standalone lanes or one verified batch-child lane), per-lane merge, canonical reconcile, and close-ready evidence only.",
      "Dispatch exactly the effective worker count: two host-created Codex Desktop mf_sub workers in one atomic bounded_workers payload for standalone mf_parallel, or one non-atomic worker for a verified batch-child contract. Each worker has a distinct RuntimeContext, task, worker slot, worktree, branch, merge queue, and owned_files fence.",
      "Before initial mf_sub allocation, call parallel_branch_allocate_precheck using the effective allocation-precheck policy: exactly two atomic lanes for standalone mf_parallel, or exactly one non-atomic lane per verified batch-child contract. Copy every returned copy_safe_allocation_body unchanged into parallel_branch_allocate; do not manually compose route, task, worktree, branch, merge-queue, or acceptance identity.",
      "Allocation precheck and every Drift Gym checkpoint are read-only. The precheck must perform zero RuntimeContext, worktree, merge-queue, timeline, and ContractRuntime writes; caller-supplied external paths are diagnostics only and are projected to the registered repository .worktrees directory.",
      "Every selected worker owns its own read receipt, startup, graph trace, implementation, worker commit, finish-time attestation, and finish gate evidence. Every worker line uses its runtime_context line_instance_id.",
      "Do not advance to merge until every required worker line instance has passed finish gate. Merge each lane through its own durable merge queue, then reconcile the final canonical HEAD exactly once.",
      "Independent integration QA runs only after all required lane merges and the activated canonical reconcile. QA must test and query the final canonical HEAD/reconciled graph, never a worker worktree or historical fixture.",
      "Authenticated independent QA alone authors PASS or NO-PASS. QA NO-PASS keeps the parent open and allocates exactly one bounded failed_qa_rework worker tied to the failed QA source on the same append-only mf_parallel execution; it does not repeat the initial required-lane fan-out. After repair it returns through merge, reconcile, and a fresh QA session. direct_fix is forbidden.",
      "Before implementation, compare each persisted owned_files fence with worker-authored files. Inherited target-head files are not worker-authored files and must not be added to changed_files.",
      "A worker scope-insufficiency request is append-only sideband evidence, not authority. Never widen owned_files from the request itself.",
      "Merge materialize uses durable status merge_ready. If live apply proves a candidate is already contained, retain the canonical observer merge event with git_mutation_executed=false.",
      "Post-merge graph_current_full_reconcile activate=true requires durable merge authority for all required lanes and a distinct activation snapshot id.",
      "An accepted worker_commit is immutable within its lane and execution. Final QA NO-PASS may allocate exactly one fresh append-only failed_qa_rework RuntimeContext; it never reopens, replaces, or supersedes the accepted worker_commit.",
      "The only legacy terminal supersession admitted by rev10 is the exact source/state/checkpoint declared by system_layer.terminal_supersession_policy. That transition records superseded_no_pass on the old generation and reserves exactly one fresh two-lane rev10 generation; old lines, traces, credentials, QA, commits, worktrees, and merge queues never carry forward.",
      "A terminal supersession replay is transport-idempotent only for the exact typed request. Any source, state, checkpoint, base, generation, authority, or cardinality mismatch is a zero-write refusal. The old execution remains terminal and can never project implementation, retry, resume, merge, QA, or close authority.",
      "Copy only copy-safe route and runtime references. Never persist raw route, session, or fence tokens."
    ],
    "refs": []
  },
